## Before you begin

This page is intentionally short. A real getting-started guide should get the reader to one visible success before explaining every option.

Copy the environment file:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Set the public URL and support address:

```env
APP_URL=http://localhost:8090
SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@example.com
```

## Run the application

```bash
task dev
```

Open the local URL printed by the task. The application and asset watchers reload as files change.

## Verify the first request

```bash
curl --include http://localhost:8090/healthz
```

The health endpoint returns an empty `204 No Content` response:

```text
HTTP/1.1 204 No Content
```

Replace this sample with the shortest path to your product's first meaningful result.
